339	// resolvePushCommandTarget returns the target to pass to git push. When a
340	// dedicated checkpoint_remote is configured, the checkpoint URL is returned so
341	// the push is routed to the separate checkpoint repo. Otherwise the remote
342	// name is returned unchanged so git uses its own config, updates the
343	// refs/remotes/<name>/<branch> tracking ref, and subsequent calls can use that
344	// tracking ref to skip redundant pushes.
